reward text Profession recipes at Friendly and Honored
why Forever's trade camps: their best recipes, the Minimule and the Pack Kodo need standing, not only Merchant's Favor.

# Azeroth Commerce Authority (2586, Alliance) and Durotar Supply and Logistics
# (2587, Horde): Forever's trade camps. Each side earns only its own camp's
# standing (Forever's faction table locks the other side's at the bottom).
# Built from Forever's quest pages (reputation per quest: Shipping Label
# 98247/98248 2000 once; Crate Return 93862 50; the 150 Craftsman's Writs
# 94004-94360, all daily, 45 at 75, 60 at 125 and 45 at 200; the four
# "A Sealed Crate" quests give no reputation, only Merchant's Favor), the
# pages' writ customers (43 of the 45 Journeyman writs and one Expert writ;
# the other Expert and Artisan customers are not in the data, the beta
# stopped at level 30), npcs.json for the camps, the drop data for the writ
# envelopes (Sealed Journeyman's Writ from 173 world mobs of level 11-31),
# and Forever's client item table for the rewards it gates by standing
# (Advertising License Application Honored, the tabards Exalted).
# The Merchant's Favor prices, the Revered Packmule Treat, the Exalted Pack
# Kodo and the scribes' items (Forged Delivery Receipt at Friendly, Forger's
# Quill at Honored) are vendor rules the item table does not hold: they
# follow several beta reports that agree. Polestar cannot count Merchant's
# Favor. Numbers are base reputation; the Legacy perk Diplomat adds up to
# 10%. Every quest here is level 60, so no level cut applies. The Legacy perk
# Performance Bonus raises Merchant's Favor from crates, not reputation.
# ASSUMED: Crate Return (93862) is handed to Marcy Baker or Dokimi from their
# window (Classic-style repeatable; Forever's data names no giver). In-game
# check: who takes the Notarized Shipping Container.
# ASSUMED: Journeyman writs keep paying 75 past Honored (Forever's quest data
# gives the writs no standing limit). In-game check: a Journeyman writ turned
# in at Honored or above.

step Your first Waylaid Crate or writ
  tip From level 10, mobs anywhere drop Waylaid Crates and sealed writs (Journeyman's, Expert's and Artisan's). Fill a crate with one of the bundles it lists (right-click it), or open a sealed writ: by beta reports, the first time you do either you also get a Shipping Label. Right-click the label to start its quest. Crates and writs can be traded, so the Auction House sells them too.
  accept 98247 only Alliance
  accept 98248 only Horde

step Three Corners: the Shipping Label
  only Alliance
  zone Redridge Mountains
  tip The Azeroth Commerce Authority camp is at Three Corners, where the roads from Elwynn Forest, Duskwood and Lakeshire meet in western Redridge. The label pays 2000 reputation once (and, by beta reports, 50 Merchant's Favor): two thirds of the way to Friendly. Filled crates go to Marcy Baker too, but they pay only Merchant's Favor and silver, never reputation.
  turnin 98247

step The Crossroads camp: the Shipping Label
  only Horde
  zone The Barrens
  tip The Durotar Supply and Logistics camp stands just outside the west gate of the Crossroads. The label pays 2000 reputation once (and, by beta reports, 50 Merchant's Favor): two thirds of the way to Friendly. Filled crates go to Dokimi too, but they pay only Merchant's Favor and silver, never reputation.
  turnin 98248

step Gather your writs
  tip Craftsman's Writs are the camp's reputation: 75 for a Journeyman writ, 125 for an Expert, 200 for an Artisan. Each asks for one crafted item, named in its quest (not always the writ's title: a Lesser Troll's Blood Elixir writ wants a Strong Troll's Blood Potion). Make it or buy it on the Auction House; you need not know the profession. Each writ can be done once a day, and any number of different ones. Take the quest only of writs whose item you have or will buy on the way (right-click the writ), keep the writ in your bags, then tick this: the next steps lead to each customer you hold a writ for.
  task "Take the quests of the writs you can fill"

step Duskwood writ customers
  when onquest 94214,94232,94241,94250
  zone Duskwood
  tip Kzixx stands about 450 yards north of Darkshire. Customers show no quest mark: right-click them anyway.
  turnin 94214 npc 3134                       -- Shadow Protection Potion, 75 reputation
  turnin 94232 npc 3134                       -- Minor Recombobulator, 75 reputation
  turnin 94241 npc 3134                       -- Dark Leather Tunic, 75 reputation
  turnin 94250 npc 3134                       -- Small Silk Pack, 75 reputation

step Stranglethorn Vale writ customers
  when onquest 94226,94235,94244,94217,94253
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip Booty Bay holds three customers: "Sea Wolf" MacKinley, Scooty, the goblin transporter's engineer, and Narkk. Short John Mithril stands at the Gurubashi Arena, about 800 yards south of Grom'gol; Hekshi is in northern Stranglethorn. Customers show no quest mark: right-click them anyway.
  turnin 94226 npc 2501                       -- Green Iron Gauntlets, 75 reputation
  turnin 94235 npc 7853                       -- Gnomish Universal Remote, 75 reputation
  turnin 94244 npc 2663                       -- Dark Leather Shoulders, 75 reputation
  turnin 94217 npc 14508                      -- Strong Troll's Blood Potion, 75 reputation
  turnin 94253 npc 261961                     -- Colorful Kilt, 75 reputation

